Ithkuil is not a Loglan derivative, indeed it's not even a loglang,
although it is an engelang. And Ithkuil was never meant to be spoken by
anyone. It's a proof-of-concept project.

For myself, if Lojban (or even Loglan) is 'good enough', then so is any
natlang. I'd rather start from scratch, using knowledge gained from
previous attempts, than continue learning or using a language that is
merely 'good enough'.

stevo

